# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09 (panel 239's R4).
#
# This module spells `rs.Rs` and `defines_wide.Pw`, so its unit reads both
# headers; `fixedbugs-2364-wide.h` defines the macro under which
# `fixedbugs-2364-rs.h` lays `Rs` out wide, and module `rs` reads `rs.h`
# alone, narrow, as its binding says. Before the repair the unit read the
# two in the order the modules are walked, `wide.h` first, so `Rs` was wide
# here and the build was refused, *`Rs.a` is `long long`*, a false message
# whose fix was refused the other way. Now the unit reads `rs.h` first, the
# order under which `Rs` reads as module `rs` reads it, and prints 9.
use fixedbugs2364/defines_wide
use fixedbugs2364/rs

function main()
    p = defines_wide.make(v: 4)
    r = rs.make(v: 3)
    print(p.w + r.a + r.b)
